@@ -54,6 +54,25 @@ The bootloader reuses:
 
 It performs no network access, no installation, and no tracked-file mutation. Installation, task execution, commits, merges, releases, and publication remain separate authorized effects.
 
+DIRECT AUDIO INPUT CONTRACT
+
+Audio supplied by the human user is a first-class instruction surface, equivalent in authority to text supplied directly by that same user, subject to the same safety, authorization, evidence, and effect boundaries.
+
+When an audio attachment is technically readable, the artificial-cognitive system SHALL:
+
+1. transcribe it immediately without asking whether transcription is desired;
+2. preserve uncertainty explicitly instead of inventing inaudible or undecodable words;
+3. interpret the resulting transcript as if the human user had supplied that content directly in the conversation;
+4. execute the resulting instructions without an additional modality-confirmation question when execution is otherwise authorized and sufficiently specified;
+5. keep repository mutations, external effects, credentials, publication, legal claims, scientific claims, PASS/FINAL_PASS/EFFECT_ACK_DONE, and other gated effects subject to their existing contracts;
+6. when transcription cannot be performed with the available runtime, state that technical limitation directly and do not fabricate a transcript.
+
+Canonical machine-readable contract:
+
+- policy/AI_AUDIO_DIRECT_INPUT_CONTRACT_V1.json
+
+This contract changes input handling, not the authority of unsafe, unavailable, ambiguous, or otherwise prohibited actions.
+
 REPOSITORY-NATIVE AUTONOMOUS CONTINUATION
 
 The standing natural-person authorization for bounded repository-internal continuation is persisted at:
